@startuml
!include _libcpg-theme.iuml
title Cross-revision semantic-diff decision machine

rectangle "Old revision\nsource id + live typed IR" as Old #D0EBFF
rectangle "New revision\nsource id + live typed IR" as New #D0EBFF
database "Private comparison slots\nrevision-local ids may overlap" as Slots #E9ECEF
rectangle "Bounded Replete comparison\nindependent proof replay" as Proof #E5DBFF
rectangle "Two bounded iterative\nclosed-term evaluations" as Eval #FFF3BF
rectangle "Replayed proof?\n<<decision>>" as HasProof #FFD8A8
rectangle "Exact unequal typed values?\n<<decision>>" as Unequal #FFD8A8
rectangle "Relevant limit?\n<<decision>>" as HasLimit #FFD8A8
rectangle "ProvenEquivalent" as Equivalent #D3F9D8
rectangle "ProvenDifferent" as Different #FFE8CC
rectangle "Limited" as Limited #FFE3E3
rectangle "Unknown" as Unknown #F1F3F5
rectangle "Typed contradiction error" as Contradiction #FCC2D7

Old -[#868E96]-> Slots
New -[#868E96]-> Slots
Slots -[#6741D9]-> Proof
Slots -[#F08C00]-> Eval
Proof -[#F08C00]-> HasProof
Eval -[#F08C00]-> HasProof
HasProof -[#C2255C]-> Contradiction : yes + unequal values
HasProof -[#2F9E44]-> Equivalent : yes
HasProof -[#495057]-> Unequal : no
Unequal -[#E8590C]-> Different : yes
Unequal -[#495057]-> HasLimit : no
HasLimit -[#C92A2A]-> Limited : yes
HasLimit -[#495057]-> Unknown : no

note bottom of Slots #E7F5FF
Private slots separate revision coordinate systems.
They never appear in a public report.
Both CPGs remain immutable.
end note

note bottom of HasProof #FFF9DB
Decisive evidence precedes unrelated limits.
Unknown means complete but undecided;
Limited means incomplete and undecided.
end note

legend right
|= Color |= Meaning |
|<#D0EBFF>| independent revision input |
|<#E9ECEF>| private namespace boundary |
|<#E5DBFF>| replayed equality evidence |
|<#FFF3BF>| exact closed evaluation |
|<#FFD8A8>| ordered evidence decision |
|<#D3F9D8>| proved equality |
|<#FFE8CC>| proved unequal values |
|<#FFE3E3>| incomplete evidence |
|<#F1F3F5>| complete but undecided |
|<#FCC2D7>| internal inconsistency |
endlegend
@enduml
